{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-quantum-universe-exists","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:quantum-universe-exists","kind":"proposition","title":"Existence of quantum universes","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-universe","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-rigid-monoidal-vect"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-quantum-universe-exists"],"tags":["existence","quantum-universe"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.QuantumUniverse.exists_instance","text":"quantum-universe-exists.md","leanSource":"quantum-universe-exists.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"prop:quantum-universe-exists\"></a>\n<strong>Proposition.</strong> <em>Existence of quantum universes</em></p>\n<p>The four <a href=\"#def:quantum-universe\">quantum universe</a> axioms are jointly satisfiable. There exists a triple <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> satisfying them.</p>\n"}
